  "body": "Add bounded 2D swallowtail healing via an explicit `heal_tolerance` parameter on `WireRuled` (`crates/motion/src/wire_edm/`).\n\n## Context\n\nToday `Region::offset_sharp` (`crates/geometry/src/geo2d.rs`) already trims local inside-corner swallowtails and bridges dead-end slots on a single 2D loop. Then `laws::cover` (`crates/motion/src/wire_edm/laws.rs`) refuses any point where `d - k > COVER_TOL` (`0.002 mm`).\n\n## What this does\n\n- Add `heal_tolerance: f64` (default `0.0`) to `WireRuled` (`crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ruled.rs`), distinct from twist `tolerance`.\n- Refuse negative or non-finite `heal_tolerance` at the `wire_contour_ruled` door.\n- Pass `reach = k + r.heal_tolerance.max(COVER_TOL)` into `laws::cover` on both planes (`ruled.rs` and `ruled_widen.rs`) while keeping `laws::kerf` (`PATH_TOL`) unchanged.\n- Measure the worst uncut rest `d - k` and its location when `d - k > COVER_TOL`.\n- If `d - k <= heal_tolerance`, accept the offset ring and push a clear uncut-corner note to `Toolpath::notes` naming the worst rest and spot.\n- If `d - k > heal_tolerance`, keep the named refusal with the spot, measured depth `d - k`, and stated `heal_tolerance`.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- `wire_contour_ruled` with `heal_tolerance == 0.0` preserves all existing refusals byte for byte.\n- Matching tight inside corners and shallow slots within `heal_tolerance > 0.0` generate valid paths with uncut-rest notes in `Toolpath::notes`, and paths still pass `laws::kerf`, `folds`, `crossing`, `clearance`, and `lean_law`.\n- Excesses above `heal_tolerance` refuse by name with location and depth.\n\nPart of #2690\n",
